WEBVTT

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:32.170
<b>Scorching</b>

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:32.170
<b>Ping Pong Girls</b>

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.420
Now, make your choice.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.620
Let's see if you're back in form.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.240
Th-Thank oo f-for coming tobay!

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:16.680
<i>Tongue-tied.</i>

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.350
I will simply beat them to death!

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:51.590
As promised, you can have whichever
rubber you want as thanks for your help.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.630
Now, make your choice.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.550
Come on, come on!

00:01:55.550 --> 00:02:00.930
Y-You can't just spring this on me!
I don't know which to pick!

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:03.970
Oh, well.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:09.350
I'll pick the perfect rubber
for you, Peach Panties.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.530
<b>Seventh Serve</b>

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.530
<b>National Caliber</b>

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.180
Okay, then, Koyori.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:26.030
Let's see if you're back in form.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:26.790
'Kay!

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.160
What kind of rubber did you pick for her?

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:33.790
Koyori-chan's biggest weapon is her smash,

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.080
so a nice and springy one?

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:37.870
No.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.760
What I picked for Peach Panties

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.100
was a rubber that makes
every hit feel pleasant.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.770
This rubber, more than any other,

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.940
gives out a sharp,
exhilarating clank when you hit the ball.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:59.750
Sure, a springy rubber
can make your smash more lethal.

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:00.910
But...

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.120
Amazing!

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.410
Peach Panties's table tennis
rises and falls with her feelings,

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:10.830
so I thought a more responsive rubber
would better help her get in the mood.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:16.340
That maybe she'd enjoy the game even more.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.920
<i>Wow! Amazing!</i>

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:22.300
<i>No rubber I've ever used
has made my shots feel this good!</i>

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:24.510
Looks like you're finally back.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.600
That's more like my Koyori.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.420
A choice that prioritizes fun, huh?

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.980
Yeah, that rubber
is perfect for Koyori-chan.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:40.570
A choice you couldn't make
unless you really understood her.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.790
You're so nice, Hokuto.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.850
Of course!

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.770
Right, Hokuto?

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.540
Hokuto-san.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:54.250
U-Uh, thank you.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:58.210
Y-You're welcome.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:04.720
Okay, now that Koyori-chan's back in form,

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.040
let's get some intensive training in
for the practice match!

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.560
Yeah!

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.890
<b>Day of the Practice Match</b>

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:15.560
So this is Mozuyama Junior High.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.450
Let's go, girls.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:21.650
Yeah.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:28.780
Pleasure to meet you!

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.210
I'm Zakuro, captain of the
Mozuyama Junior High Table Tennis Team!

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:37.880
Th-Thank oo f-for coming tobay!

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.120
<i>Tongue-tied.</i>

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:39.790
<i>Tongue-tied.</i>

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:41.090
<i>Tongue-tied.</i>

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:45.520
I'm Ushirode Kiruka, captain of the
Suzumegahara Junior High Table Tennis Team.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.770
Thank you very much for having us.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.100
Let's have a good, productive session today.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.730
Y-Y-Yes, let's!

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:56.790
<i>The practice match is about to start.</i>

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.980
Okay, it's almost time for our
practice match with Mozuyama,

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:09.750
a team that went to Nationals.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:13.390
Let's give it our all
and make this match one to remember!

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:14.160
Yes!

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.600
We're here to win and gain some momentum
heading into tournament play in summer,

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.530
but that's only part of the goal.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:25.760
The other part is to see
just how good we are right now.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:26.630
Right!

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:30.730
Okay, warm up fully before play begins.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.090
Got it!

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.660
They're all up for it.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:36.630
As am I.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:39.770
I'm really happy I can play doubles
with you after all this time.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.760
Jeez, not again.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:51.750
Can't wait to find out
how we compare, huh?

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:53.860
Yep.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:59.250
Also, we have high hopes for you
as our new, rising star, Koyori-chan!

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:00.870
R-Right.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.590
I'm deathly sorry.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.930
Could you pick up that dead ball?

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.450
Sure.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:21.950
You're...

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:25.570
Do you know her, Koyori?

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:28.130
I don't exactly <i>know</i> her,

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:31.800
but we met while I was
helping at Hokuto-san's store.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.510
I'm surprised to death.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:35.620
I never expected you
to be one of our opponents...

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:37.850
You remember me?

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:39.080
...pregnant attendant girl.

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:43.710
Y-You've got it all wrong!
I'm not pregnant!

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:48.420
But you looked like death at the register,
with your "hee, hee, hoo."

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:50.380
Th-That...

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:54.640
Th-That's because Hokuto-san said
it'd help me relax!

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.750
Is death so?

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.560
Well, it deathn't matter who I'm up against.

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:05.110
Anyone and everyone who comes at us...

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.030
I will simply beat them to death!

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:19.490
That's how it's always been,

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:22.720
and that's how it'll always be.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:30.670
We will win today
and grant you death, too.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.680
I'm deathly thankful to you for the ball.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:38.540
Wh-What was that all about?

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:41.000
She just declared war on us, huh?

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:43.860
She's pumping out this
ominous aura at full power!

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:45.230
It's bad for the heart.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:48.550
I've seen her play before,

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:52.120
but I didn't know she was always like that.

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:53.950
Is she famous?

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:57.240
That's putting it mildly.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.490
She's Futamaru Kururi, Driver of the East,

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:04.540
and the player who led
Mozuyama Junior High to Nationals.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:08.380
All right, girls, it's time
to play Suzumegahara.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.000
It may only be a practice match,

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.140
but we're gonna treat it like
an official match and fight to the death!

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:16.300
Y-Yes!

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.170
Huh? What's gotten into you all?

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:21.170
You're talking in falsetto.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:25.500
R-Relax. "Fight to the death"
was only a figure of speech.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:26.440
Wait, Kururi?

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:30.600
Oh, come on! I keep telling you
not to intimidate our juniors!

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.780
I-It wasn't on purpose! I swear to death!

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.900
Y-You were dropping pearls of wisdom
about fighting to the death.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:40.510
So I was just gesturing with my eyes
that they should pay attention,

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:42.830
even if they were warming up.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.960
Y-You don't have to
go out of your way to do that.

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:53.880
But, as vice-captain, it is my duty
to support you to death!

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.720
A-Anyway, let's give it our all, girls!

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:59.110
Take down Suzumegahara!

00:08:59.110 --> 00:09:02.470
Let's show them the skills
that took us to Nationals!

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:03.980
Yes!

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.440
Your ribbon's deathly crooked.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:12.140
Your shirt's all crumpled, too.
Pull it together, or you'll die.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:16.680
This morning, you walked down the stairs
with your butt instead of your legs

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:19.870
and nearly left for school
wearing different shoes on each foot.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:25.250
You're really clumsy if left alone,
so I'm worried to death.

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:29.770
J-Jeez, you make me sound like a goofball!

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:31.790
You weren't aware? Deathness me.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.720
But thanks, Kururi...

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:45.100
For always having my back.

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:53.720
<i>She thanked... Zakuro thanked me!</i>

00:09:56.540 --> 00:10:00.720
<i>Is this real life, or is it death?</i>

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:02.560
But, you know,

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.830
don't just worry about me all the time.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.000
Look after yourself—

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:09.170
Kururi?

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.370
Kururi?!

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:12.090
Can you hear me?!

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.440
Sheesh.

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:16.020
When they act like that all the time,

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:20.720
it's hard to believe they're two of the best
table tennis players in the nation.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:25.090
But I, the future captain,

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:28.350
Second-Year: "The Scorpion" Sasorida

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:28.350
am about the only one
who can face them on equal terms!

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.270
Second-Year: "The Pendulum" Yuragi

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:30.270
I don't think that's happening.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:32.290
Second-Year: "Broke" Kanenashi

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:31.880
Not happening.

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:32.810
Mod habbeninf!

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:34.790
Second-Year: "Nom-Nom" Kimiko

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:37.340
Wh-Why do you all have to
rain on my parade?!

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:38.740
Dammit!

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:40.250
Huh?

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:43.990
Mozuyama's appearance in last
summer's Nationals was their first?

00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:46.030
Yeah.

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:49.430
They used to be an average team,

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:53.000
but Futamaru-san turned them
into one that can go to Nationals.

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:58.320
But, for all the tables they have here,
I don't see many members.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:01.340
What's more, they only have two third-years.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:02.350
Only two?!

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:04.850
Yeah. Those two playing over there.

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:07.810
Futamaru-san and Zakuro-san.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:11.880
The two of them led their juniors
all by themselves and went to Nationals.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:13.480
It's amazing.

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:18.540
The two of them
must have a really strong bond.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:22.450
<i>Players who led their team to Nationals...</i>

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:25.680
<i>Strong bond, huh?</i>

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.510
<i>I'm not worried to death about my form.</i>

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.120
<i>I'm dead sure I'll win today.</i>

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:44.460
<i>No matter what the match
or who the opponent is,</i>

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:47.470
<i>until the day I die, that is my duty.</i>

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:49.260
We did it, Kururi!

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:00.680
<i>The smile on Zakuro's face when I win...</i>

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:04.550
<i>My heart is about to burst
just imagining it.</i>

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:11.710
<i>If I actually win,
I bet it'll feel even better...</i>

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:14.540
My heart's about to burst!

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:21.470
A pervert?

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:22.910
Help me!

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:25.980
U-Uh, I got up here, but I can't get down.

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:29.850
C-Could you please lend me a hand?

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:36.280
The lock on my stall's door was broken,
and I got trapped inside!

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:38.670
I-I knew I shouldn't have,

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:41.530
but I figured I could sneakily climb out!

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:45.290
S-So, uh...

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:47.990
Thank you for helping me!

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:52.010
You're welcome... to death.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:56.700
Tail! Tail! Tail! Tail!

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.110
You seem to be enjoying yourself to death.

00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:58.290
I-I am!

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:02.690
U-Uh, I'm Tsumujikaze Koyori.

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:05.100
I'll be playing
in the practice match today,

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:09.270
and thinking about what kind of person
I'll face got my heart racing.

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:12.510
U-Um, if we end up playing each other,

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:14.710
l-let's have fun!

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.480
I hope we have a good game!

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:22.740
A good game? Is death so?

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:28.990
Not even death would make that enough
to pay the friendship fee.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.580
Friendship fee?

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:33.400
Kururi?

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:34.500
Oh, there you are.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:36.830
The match is about to begin.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:37.920
Let's hurry back now.

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:43.350
Tsumujikaze-san, was it?

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:47.930
Why do you play
the life-or-death game of table tennis?

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:51.220
I play for her!

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.380
I can offer up all I have for Zakuro!

00:13:57.380 --> 00:13:59.810
I'm prepared to die!

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.770
Wait, what? Where did that come from?

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:10.240
Nothing. I just saved
a very active pregnant girl from death.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:12.590
Let's go bring death upon them.

00:14:12.590 --> 00:14:14.140
O-Okay.

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.130
<i>Offer up everything?</i>

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.790
<i>What I play table tennis for?</i>

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:23.410
<i>What </i>do<i> I play for?</i>

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:30.390
We will now begin the practice match
between Suzumegahara and Mozuyama.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:32.840
Let's have a good game!

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:39.930
It's almost time
for the practice match to begin.

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:44.050
Say, how do team play matches work, again?

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:47.320
Er, Agari-senpai was saying earlier

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:51.980
that junior high team play is comprised of
four singles matches and one doubles match.

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:57.790
Singles 1

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:57.790
Singles 2

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:57.790
Singles 3

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:57.790
Singles 4

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:57.790
Doubles

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:57.790
1st Match

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:57.790
2nd Match

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:57.790
3rd Match

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:57.790
4th Match

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:57.790
5th Match

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:53.820
It's a best-of-five,

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:56.430
so the first team
that takes three matches wins.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:59.790
Suzumegahara vs. Mozuyama
S1: Tenka Hanabi vs. Sasorida Sachiko
S2: Itsumo Hokuto vs. Yuragi Yura
D: Ushirode Kiruka/Munemune vs. Kanenashi Mayuu/Hamu Kimiko
S3: Kamiya Agari vs. Zashikiwarashi Zakuro
S4: Tsumujikaze Koyori vs. Futamaru Kururi

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:03.840
<b>S4: Tsumujikaze Koyori vs. Futamaru Kururi</b>

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:07.120
Koyori.

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:08.080
Koyori?

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:09.300
Koyori!

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:13.120
Jeez, what are you spacing out for?

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:18.090
Your opponent is the Driver of the East!

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:21.370
Mozuyama's ace!

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:22.400
Do you get it?!

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:27.150
Why do you play
the life-or-death game of table tennis?

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:29.940
Koyori?

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:37.660
All right! Here I go!

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.630
Break a leg, Hanabi.

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:40.970
Good luck!

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:42.420
Do your best, Hanabi.

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:47.000
So, who am I up against?

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:53.000
Hey, give me some
words of encouragement here!

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:55.970
It doesn't matter whether you win or lose.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:57.460
Doesn't matter.

00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:58.470
Ja!

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:03.500
What's wrong with you guys?
I'm your future captain, y'know?!

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:03.710
They seem kind of relaxed.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:05.190
No tension.

00:16:05.890 --> 00:16:07.860
Tenka versus Sasorida.

00:16:08.290 --> 00:16:09.690
Best-of-five match.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.140
First game.

00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:12.840
Tenka to serve.

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:14.490
Love-all!

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:15.740
Take that!

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:22.540
One-love.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:23.670
Okay!

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:25.440
Yay!

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:27.250
Hanabi-senpai scored first!

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:34.850
There!

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:40.100
Wow!

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:41.680
That's our Hanabi-senpai!

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:49.440
Why do you play
the life-or-death game of table tennis?

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.240
Wow, already?

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:00.440
Well, Hanabi is all about speed.

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:04.100
She's probably the best at
Suzumegahara in terms of speed.

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:08.210
J-Just speed! Just speed!

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:11.090
All right!

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:18.390
Second game.

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:20.390
Sasorida to serve.

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:21.600
Love-all.

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:28.940
How d'you like that?

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:30.890
Wow, awesome!

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:32.650
She might win in straight games!

00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:42.880
I don't think a comeback's happening.

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:44.090
Not happening.

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:44.970
Mod habbeninf!

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:47.750
Hey, cheer me on!

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:50.570
Third game.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:52.310
Tenka to serve.

00:17:52.310 --> 00:17:53.290
Love-all.

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:57.090
Okay, it's high time I dug in.

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:03.260
The first point is hers!

00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:18.450
Love-one.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.820
She caught me by surprise.

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:22.950
Again?

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:24.740
You little...

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:27.610
Yet again?

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:30.710
Oh, come on!

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:32.040
Eat this!

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:34.590
Here.

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:38.680
Two-love.

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.550
She's throwing me off-rhythm!

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:55.200
Kiruka, how does she compare to you?

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.400
Well, she's a pretty damn good chopper.

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:01.530
<i>It'll bounce high again!</i>

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:05.790
Three-love.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:08.410
I can't drag her into a battle of speed!

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:14.420
Eleven-nine. Game to Sasorida.

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:19.940
Eleven-eight. Game to Sasorida.

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:22.960
Final game.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:24.680
Tenka to serve.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:25.910
Love-all.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:29.770
I-I'm running out of gas.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:35.790
Huh?

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:38.400
Looks like you fell for my trap.

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:40.280
At this point,

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:44.280
you are but sad prey,
rendered immobile in a scorching hot desert.

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:52.250
Okay, the table is all set.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.670
Now, I'll just take my time

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:01.470
and dig in.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:03.430
Eek!

00:20:14.050 --> 00:20:16.400
Damn you!

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:19.200
<i>I can't drag her</i>

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:21.040
<i>into a battle of speed</i>

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:22.530
<i>close to the table...</i>

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:34.990
Eleven-three.

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:37.670
Game and match to Sasorida!

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:40.920
I lost.

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:46.210
Hanabi completely lost the initiative.

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:50.600
By nullifying her favorite speed drives,
she forced her to make errors.

00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:53.760
Even if you hop around so as
not to be burned by the desert sands,

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:56.380
you'll run out of gas eventually.

00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:01.230
That's right! You cannot run from a hunter!

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:03.320
You need the skills to beat them!

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:15.710
How's that? I gave us
the best start possible!

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:20.670
Not very good.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.050
No good.

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:23.170
Mo' food.

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:26.880
Wh-What? What wasn't good about it?!

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:31.050
Hanabi.

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:33.190
Sorry, Hokuto.

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:34.350
I went and lost.

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:36.060
Don't worry.

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:38.690
I'll avenge your loss.

00:21:40.450 --> 00:21:42.150
Yeah. I'm counting on you.

00:21:45.590 --> 00:21:47.530
I don't think that's happening.

00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:51.990
Eleven-three.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:53.900
Game to Yuragi.

00:22:05.690 --> 00:22:08.090
So this is what Mozuyama's like.

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:11.310
This is what national caliber is!

00:23:43.860 --> 00:24:00.000
Preview

00:23:45.050 --> 00:23:46.480
Zakuro's words are life-or-death.

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:48.400
Talk about a mean streak.

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:49.090
Our training is leagues apart.

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:50.110
She really is predicting my moves!

00:23:49.090 --> 00:23:51.400
It is happening!

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:52.860
Can you really win?

00:23:52.050 --> 00:23:54.070
I can win, yes!

00:23:54.070 --> 00:23:56.370
Her smashes can't break through.

00:23:55.070 --> 00:23:57.330
I want a meat bun now.
